1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,045
The mountain
down your

2
00:00:01,045 --> 00:00:02,905
street just
exploded.

3
00:00:02,905 --> 00:00:04,970
It's not the
only one.

4
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:06,950
Every volcano that
could erupt did,

5
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:09,120
all around
the planet.

6
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,450
You can walk away
from most lava.

7
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:12,900
Avalanches
of hot

8
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,220
ash can
outrun a car.

9
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,740
You're one of
800 million

10
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,970
people living
near a volcano.

11
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:20,160
Within days,

12
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,060
you're sweeping
up the ash.

13
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,050
But the sun
stays dim.

14
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,580
The biggest
blasts lifted

15
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,820
sulfur twenty
kilometers up.

16
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,440
It hangs there
for a year,

17
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:31,670
bouncing sunlight
back to space.

18
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:33,630
One volcano,
Tambora,

19
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:36,410
did this
in 1815.

20
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,230
A year later,

21
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:38,510
it snowed in
New England.

22
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:39,970
In June.

23
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,350
All these
eruptions together

24
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:43,650
could lift even
more sulfur.

25
00:00:43,650 --> 00:00:45,270
Northern summers
could fail,

26
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:47,380
and the harvest
with them.

27
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:50,260
The lava stays near
the mountains.

28
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:52,310
The cold reaches
everyone.
